## macOS-specific shell extensions. POSIX-compliant.
## Sourced from .profile when `uname -s` is Darwin.

## SSH agent: macOS runs a launchd-managed ssh-agent (com.openssh.ssh-agent).
## SSH_AUTH_SOCK is inherited from the user session automatically — no
## per-shell `eval "$(ssh-agent -s)"` needed.
##
## To get lazy, on-first-use key loading with Keychain-stored passphrase:
##
##   1. Add to ~/.ssh/config (or create via `Include` from dotfiles):
##        Host *
##          AddKeysToAgent yes
##          UseKeychain yes
##          IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
##
##   2. Seed the Keychain once (interactive, prompts for passphrase):
##        ssh-add --apple-use-keychain ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
